# Non-Critical Operation Logs

Operation logs added for audit, click tracking, or diagnostic context must not block the main business flow.

- Wrap best-effort log writes in an internal `try-catch`, especially when using `REQUIRES_NEW`, database writes, Feign calls, or MQ-side compensation logs.
- Log write failures with `log.warn(...)`; do not let them bubble into Controller batch results or MQ consumer retry paths unless the log itself is the business objective.
- In batch loops, avoid extra per-item queries only for logging. Reuse entities already loaded for the main operation, or batch load them once and pass the entity/code into the log method.

Example:

```java
try {
    operateLogService.addModuleOperateLogRequiresNew(message, moduleType, bizId, action);
} catch (Exception e) {
    log.warn("operation log write failed,bizId:{}", bizId, e);
}
```
